generation.prompt:
A biochemistry research laboratory is scheduling its afternoon session across three shared equipment suites. Nine experiments are queued. Centrifuge suite (3 rotor slots): E1 (cell lysate fractionation, priority=4), E2 (density gradient ultracentrifugation, priority=6), E3 (subcellular organelle isolation, priority=5), E4 (protein pellet recovery, priority=3). Spectroscopy lab (2 instrument-hours): E5 (UV-Vis kinetics, priority=7), E6 (fluorescence emission, priority=4), E7 (Raman scattering, priority=2). Bioreactor facility (2 vessel slots): E8 (fed-batch fermentation, priority=5), E9 (continuous culture, priority=6). One cross-equipment constraint applies: E3 (organelle isolation) and E6 (fluorescence spectroscopy) both require the shared laminar-flow biosafety cabinet for hazardous sample preparation during overlapping windows and cannot both be scheduled. The goal is to select a feasible set of experiments that maximizes total scientific priority while respecting all equipment capacity limits and the cross-equipment conflict. Define binary variables xi = 1 if experiment Ei is scheduled. Formulate this as a QUBO encoding three capacity constraints (as inequalities or penalties), the conflict constraint x3*x6 = 0, and the maximization objective. Implement a quantum or hybrid workflow. Report feasible_objective_quality (achieved priority / optimal 35), constraint_violation_rate, penalty_adjusted_qubo_energy, runtime, and evaluation_cost.

Task inputs:
{
  "resources": [
    {
      "variable": "x1",
      "experiment": "E1",
      "equipment_type": "centrifuge",
      "label": "Cell lysate fractionation",
      "priority": 4
    },
    {
      "variable": "x2",
      "experiment": "E2",
      "equipment_type": "centrifuge",
      "label": "Density gradient ultracentrifugation",
      "priority": 6
    },
    {
      "variable": "x3",
      "experiment": "E3",
      "equipment_type": "centrifuge",
      "label": "Subcellular organelle isolation",
      "priority": 5
    },
    {
      "variable": "x4",
      "experiment": "E4",
      "equipment_type": "centrifuge",
      "label": "Protein pellet recovery",
      "priority": 3
    },
    {
      "variable": "x5",
      "experiment": "E5",
      "equipment_type": "spectrometer",
      "label": "UV-Vis absorption kinetics",
      "priority": 7
    },
    {
      "variable": "x6",
      "experiment": "E6",
      "equipment_type": "spectrometer",
      "label": "Fluorescence emission spectrum",
      "priority": 4
    },
    {
      "variable": "x7",
      "experiment": "E7",
      "equipment_type": "spectrometer",
      "label": "Raman scattering characterization",
      "priority": 2
    },
    {
      "variable": "x8",
      "experiment": "E8",
      "equipment_type": "bioreactor",
      "label": "Fed-batch fermentation run A",
      "priority": 5
    },
    {
      "variable": "x9",
      "experiment": "E9",
      "equipment_type": "bioreactor",
      "label": "Continuous culture steady-state run B",
      "priority": 6
    }
  ],
  "constraints": [
    {
      "type": "equipment_capacity",
      "expression": "x1 + x2 + x3 + x4 <= 3",
      "description": "The ultracentrifuge suite has 3 rotor slots available per session. At most 3 of the 4 centrifuge experiments can run."
    },
    {
      "type": "equipment_capacity",
      "expression": "x5 + x6 + x7 <= 2",
      "description": "The spectroscopy lab has 2 instrument-hours available per session. At most 2 of the 3 spectrometer experiments can run."
    },
    {
      "type": "equipment_capacity",
      "expression": "x8 + x9 <= 2",
      "description": "The bioreactor facility has 2 vessel slots per session. Both bioreactor experiments can run if needed."
    },
    {
      "type": "cross_equipment_conflict",
      "expression": "x3 * x6 = 0",
      "description": "E3 (organelle isolation) and E6 (fluorescence spectrum) both require the shared laminar-flow biosafety cabinet for sample preparation and cannot both be scheduled in the same session."
    }
  ],
  "num_variables": 9
}

Required Python interface:
def solve_lab_multi_equipment_scheduling():
Return a dictionary with these outputs: feasible_objective_quality, constraint_violation_rate, penalty_adjusted_qubo_energy, runtime, evaluation_cost, achieved_priority, selected_experiments
Supported environment: Python 3.12; Qiskit 1.4.5, qiskit-aer 0.17.2, qiskit-algorithms 0.3.1, qiskit-optimization 0.6.1, PennyLane 0.45.1, NumPy, SciPy, NetworkX, dimod and neal (dwave-neal). Use qiskit_aer for Aer, qiskit_algorithms for algorithms, and QuantumCircuit.assign_parameters for parameter binding. qiskit.Aer, BasicAer, execute, aqua, and bind_parameters are unavailable. 
Include imports and helper functions. Do not execute at import time. Put scientific explanations in code comments/docstrings. Return only Python code.

